1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Attack with cannon, and end turn.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Dang, Hazuki, you're good!

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Okay, one more match. I'm not gonna quit until I win at least one of these.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Okay, but you realize that means you're never going home.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Wise guy, eh?

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
I can't believe we finally caught you without your sister.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Come on, you don't have to say it like that.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Hey, guys! Can we play too?

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
We've got decks and all, but I don't know. The rules are kind of hard to understand.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
You're good at this, right, Kazuki?

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Huh?

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
If you don't mind, could you teach me a few tricks?

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Oh, uh, sure.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:38,800
Uh…

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,500
Should I get to it?

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Alright.

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Oh, there we go.

18
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,000
A immortal mystery person

19
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I cannot do so much

20
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:07,000
There are a story

21
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:36,980
Thank you.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:02:06,980
Thank you.

23
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Thank you.

24
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,700
Oh, and you can still sign up the day of the event, so don't be afraid to stop by and check it out.

25
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,080
Um, cool.

26
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,040
So?

27
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:48,500
I'll be done in a few minutes. Hang tight.

28
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:48,920
Cool.

29
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:51,940
Yuzuki?

30
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:56,300
Sorry. What do you think? Are we in or what?

31
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:06,600
Participating as a selector without having a wish is more than just wrong. It's blasphemy.

32
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,920
I'm going either way.

33
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:14,680
I might even find another selector to battle.

34
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,820
Yeah, but my wish already.

35
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,100
Right. It already came true.

36
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:26,240
Uh-huh. So if I won, it wouldn't be fair to the person I beat. There's no need to be greedy after all.

37
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:31,740
But if the other player isn't a selector, it'll be fine. Meaning we're free to fight all the dudes we want.

38
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:36,860
Good point. As long as nobody's dreams are at stake, I'm definitely up for a battle or two.

39
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:37,420
Yeah.

40
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:41,380
Sure. That sounds okay. I suppose I'm on board.

41
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:45,000
If nothing else, it's a chance to try out my new deck.

42
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:46,620
Right, Midoriko?

43
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:50,100
Midoriko?

44
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:50,720
Oh.

45
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:55,680
Okay, sweet!

46
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:06,680
So ladies, I was thinking about Momoka's idea for us to match our outfits. We could be like a pop-through. Huh?

47
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:10,180
That's cute, but kind of pricey.

48
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:15,100
Yeah, we spend too much on cards. Oh well.

49
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:16,700
Oh, hey, look!

50
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,120
Now that's more in our price range.

51
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:23,280
It's not quite as fancy, but we can still match with these.

52
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,180
Scrunchies, huh?

53
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:24,540
Mm-hmm.

54
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:27,700
We might not look much like a pop-through, but try it.

55
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,080
Well, you gotta go with green to match your deck.

56
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,980
Oh, cool. I found a red one.

57
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:36,400
Ruko's deck is white.

58
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:37,960
Oh, no luck.

59
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,020
You can take this weird-looking one instead.

60
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,500
Don't give me the icky one!

61
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:42,480
How's this?

62
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,360
You're picking ugly ones up perfect!

63
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:45,680
Stop it!

64
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,520
Okay, sorry.

65
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:51,900
And then we all brought these matching scrunchies.

66
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:59,680
That's lovely, and I'm thrilled that you're making new friends. But your hair is still wet from your shower. Your scrunchie is going to mess it up.

67
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:06,400
It's fine. So anyway, Ruko almost got this weird-looking one, but she ended up with Aqua instead, even though her deck is white.

68
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,640
All right, you can tell me all about it later.

69
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:12,780
But first, go dry your hair and put something warmer on. You're going to catch your death.

70
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,100
Yes, ma'am.

71
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:19,940
Aw, it did get all messed up.

72
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,480
Yeah, and the scrunchie's all damp, too!

73
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,960
Of course it is.

74
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,040
Aw, I'm so stupid.

75
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:28,360
Hitae?

76
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,000
Yeah, what is it?

77
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:32,840
I think it's best if you get rid of me.

78
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,280
Get rid of you? Why?

79
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:39,940
Your wish already came true. There's no need for you to battle anymore.

80
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:47,820
Sure, but who cares about that? I like you a whole bunch, Midoriko. I would never want to get rid of you.

81
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,600
I'm afraid that if you keep me, something might happen. Something terrible.

82
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:56,780
So what?

83
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:06,140
Before I even met Ruko and Yuzuki, you were my friend, Midoriko, and nothing will change that.

84
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:07,500
Oh, Hitoi.

85
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,880
I don't want to hear you talk like that ever again.

86
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,600
Oh, yeah! Still need to dry my hair.

87
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:22,160
Aw, I suck.

88
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,040
Something wrong?

89
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:27,920
Not really. I just can't get my hair tied up right, that's all.

90
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:31,460
You are kind of clumsy with that stuff. Here, let me get it for you.

91
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,880
Huh? No, it's fine! Really!

92
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:35,260
Don't freak out.

93
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:37,480
I'm not freaking out. I just need to learn.

94
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:43,180
It's cold.

95
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:49,400
Oh, here, look. There's a big giraffe on the building.

96
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:50,820
Cool!

97
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,640
Is it gonna battle the other giraffe?

98
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:58,540
Tama, not everything is about battles, you know.

99
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,340
I am right.

100
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:02,040
So battle me.

101
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:11,860
Iona was really pretty, but, uh, she was also kind of scary. Don't you think?

102
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:13,700
Tama can beat all the scaries!

103
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:27,660
Looks like I'm here a bit early.

104
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:31,800
I made it to the meeting spot.

105
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,760
I'll be waiting.

106
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,520
And sit.

107
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:45,380
It's funny, but when I'm standing in a big crowd like this, I almost feel like a normal girl.

108
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,680
Come on, Hitaway. You are a normal girl.

109
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,240
I'll take your word for it.

110
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,380
It's nice out.

111
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:05,380
When I first moved to Tokyo, somehow I felt like there wasn't a sky here, thanks to all the skyscrapers and stuff.

112
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:10,300
But there it is. As bright and blue as it's ever been.

113
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,200
All this time I never noticed.

114
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:15,840
How sad.

115
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,320
I just needed to look up.

116
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:20,680
Hitaway.

117
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,800
Drop me!

118
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,220
Throw me away now!

119
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:28,960
Please!

120
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,160
Hurry!

121
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:37,140
Rugo, let's go!

122
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:37,820
I'm sorry!

123
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:42,640
There were a whole bunch of people in the bathroom and the kid behind me was about to go in her pants, so I let her cut in line!

124
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,800
Hmm, we're making Hitaway wait!

125
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:45,600
Okay, okay!

126
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:47,300
Huh.

127
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,420
She said she'd be here.

128
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,720
Too short, I can't see!

129
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:59,000
Guessing you came up empty too?

130
00:08:59,100 --> 00:08:59,540
Uh-huh.

131
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,480
She isn't answering my texts either.

132
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,240
Maybe she got mad at us because we were late.

133
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:08,420
She wouldn't lose her temper over something like that.

134
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,640
Right? Back me up on this, Hanayou.

135
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:12,760
Hanayou?

136
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,780
Oh, yeah, of course.

137
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:15,420
Field!

138
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,060
Something going on, Tama?

139
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:20,340
There's a battlefield somewhere!

140
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:21,080
Close!

141
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,660
What? Around here?

142
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:24,340
Hitaway!

143
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:24,420
What?

144
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:24,500
What?

145
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:24,540
What?

146
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:24,560
What?

147
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:24,600
What?

148
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:24,620
What?

149
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:24,640
What?

150
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:24,680
What?

151
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,180
What?

152
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:25,680
What?

153
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:26,180
What?

154
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:26,680
What?

155
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:27,180
What?

156
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:27,680
What?

157
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,180
What?

158
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:28,680
What?

159
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,180
What?

160
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:30,140
What?

161
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:30,760
What?

162
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:32,940
They're strong.

163
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:34,080
Really strong!

164
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:37,520
Adyoyako!

165
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,560
I'm sorry!

166
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:39,060
No!

167
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:41,120
Don't worry about me!

168
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,020
But it's my fault!

169
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:42,540
You're suffering!

170
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:45,100
I'll try to end this quickly, okay?

171
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:46,560
I don't need to win!

172
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,320
I'll lose on purpose!

173
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,320
Please, you have to keep fighting!

174
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,320
Please, you have to keep fighting!

175
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,320
You can't give up!

176
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,320
It's fine!

177
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,320
Really!

178
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:55,320
The only wish I wanted already came true!

179
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:59,320
And now neither one of us have to go through these painful battles anymore!

180
00:09:59,320 --> 00:09:59,420
Ito-

181
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:00,320
Ito-e!

182
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,320
Ito-e!

183
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,320
Listen!

184
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,320
Huh?!

185
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,320
There's something important I haven't told you!

186
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,320
What do you mean?

187
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:10,320
You know all about winning, and becoming an eternal girl!

188
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,320
Your wish!

189
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,320
Ito-e!

190
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:19,320
Hito-e! Where did you go? Sorry, mister!

191
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,320
Hito-e!

192
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:25,320
However, you don't know what it means to lose.

193
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:58,320
Tama, we close?

194
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:02,320
The battlefield... wait, bye-bye.

195
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:07,320
Hey, Hanayo, do you know anything about this?

196
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:10,320
Hey, look!

197
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:17,320
Hito-e!

198
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,320
Hito-e!

199
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:23,320
There you are! You had us all worried!

200
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:26,320
Hito-e, what's wrong?

201
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:28,320
Wh-what do you want?

202
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:31,320
How do you know my name?

203
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:34,320
If this is a joke, I don't get it.

204
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,320
Hey, wait!

205
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:39,320
What the? Are you okay?

206
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:49,320
Hito-e! Tell us what's wrong!

207
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:57,320
Stand back! Don't touch her!

208
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:00,320
Whoever you are, leave me alone!

209
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,320
I don't-

210
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:04,320
Hito-e! Lost!

211
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:05,320
What?

212
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:08,320
Tama is not sensing her selector power!

213
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,320
She had a battle and lost!

214
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,320
No!

215
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:13,320
Are you saying she's not a selector anymore?

216
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:17,320
Did something messed up happen to her because she lost her third battle?

217
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,320
What is this?

218
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,320
Hanayo!

219
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,320
What?

220
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:29,320
After three losses, your status as a selector is revoked.

221
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:32,320
As for your wish, it becomes corrupted.

222
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,320
Ugh! You mean like you get a curse?

223
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,320
Yes.

224
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:40,320
For example, let's say your wish was to become wealthy.

225
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:46,320
After losing three battles, not only would that wish fail to come true, you would plummet into poverty.

226
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:52,320
If your wish was to be an expert pianist, you wouldn't just lose your piano.

227
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:57,320
Something would happen that would prevent you from playing ever again.

228
00:12:57,320 --> 00:13:01,320
Something to ensure your wish could never come true.

229
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,320
That's awful!

230
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,320
I'm not really getting this.

231
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,320
So what happened to Hito-e?

232
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:09,320
All I can tell you is her wish was to make friends.

233
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:13,320
You can imagine what a corruption of that would be.

234
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:16,320
So you're saying she lost her friends?

235
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:19,320
Far worse than that.

236
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:23,320
She can never make friends again.

237
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,320
You saw what state she was in.

238
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:29,320
Seems if anyone has even the potential to be her friend.

239
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:34,320
Her body goes through some sort of violent shock when they try to approach her.

240
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,320
No way!

241
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,320
Horrible.

242
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:38,320
But unfortunately, there's more.

243
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:41,320
With her third loss, not only is her selector status gone,

244
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:44,320
so are all her memories related to those battles.

245
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:47,320
As if they never even took place.

246
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:49,320
What is this?

247
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,320
What's happening?

248
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,320
I'm scared.

249
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,320
Hito-e, what's wrong?

250
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:59,320
How do they know me?

251
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,320
Who were they?

252
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,320
That didn't hurt me.

253
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:12,320
Why?

254
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,320
Why?

255
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,320
Oh God!

256
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,320
Why?

257
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,320
Why does this hurt?

258
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,320
I can't know!

259
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,320
It hurts just thinking about them.

260
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,320
They can stop!

261
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:36,320
That's it!

262
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:40,320
I'll win and wish for Hito-e to go back to normal!

263
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,320
I finally have a dream worth fighting for!

264
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,320
I didn't think of that.

265
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,320
Right!

266
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,320
It won't work.

267
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,320
What?

268
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:49,320
Even though it didn't happen as a result of winning battles,

269
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:51,320
her wish did come true.

270
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:54,320
The corruption cannot be undone by another selector's wish.

271
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:56,320
